{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>But our little ones shall dwell, etc.</b> It was necessary to say this, and moreover they did not say so above when they mentioned ״וְעָרִים לְטַפֵּנוּ״. They intended to say that if their children dwell in cities fortified as bastions, then they can add yet another condition: that they not return to their homes until each man inherits his portion — meaning, after the seven years of conquest and seven years of division pass. And if they will not be in fortified cities — meaning, cities with fortifications — but only for guard-duty as needed, they would not be confident in them to remain so long as fourteen years, but only seven years until they conquer the land. Therefore he placed the statement ״וְיָשַׁב טַפֵּנוּ בְּעָרֵי הַמִּבְצָר״ in the middle of two statements that are all one matter, namely the statement ״וַאֲנַחְנוּ נֵחָלֵץ חוּשִׁים וְגוֹ׳ עַד הֲבִיאוֹנוּם אֶל מְקוֹמָם״ and the statement ״לֹא נָשׁוּב אֶל בָּתֵּינוּ עַד הִתְנַחֵל״ וְגוֹ׳ — and it would have been proper for him to join the two statements together, since the second is a corollary of the first, and not to interrupt with something not in keeping with the subject. But according to our approach it is properly resolved." "<b>Furthermore,</b> it may be resolved why they stated two opposing boundaries: one — ״עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם הֲבִיאוֹנוּם״ וְגוֹ׳, and the second — ״עַד הִתְנַחֵל״. And although the one they said regarding the matter of ״נֵחָלֵץ חוּשִׁים״ and the second regarding the matter of returning them to their land, nevertheless from the first clause it implies that they obligated themselves only until bringing them to their place and not until the inheritance. And according to our words it is properly resolved." "And Moses said to them: ״Build you cities for your little ones,״ and he was precise in saying <b>for you</b> — meaning, according to what is in your desire, which is to build fortified cities. And so it was, as it is written: ״וַיִּבְנוּ אֶת דִּיבוֹן וְאֶת עֲטָרוֹת״ וְגוֹ׳ (Numbers 32:34–38), for these are the fortified cities — the great towns that they mentioned in their request. And you will find that they did not return to their homes until after the fourteen years of conquest and division."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:39.378329976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}